# EAS Build regenerates these on its own servers (pod install / npm
# install) -- uploading them just inflates the build archive and risks
# the upload itself timing out/dropping on a large connection, which is
# what actually failed the first production build attempt (871MB
# archive, ios/Pods alone was 1.2GB of that).
ios/Pods/
ios/build/
node_modules/
backend/node_modules/
.localnode/
.git/

# Stray marketing/store assets sitting loose in the PROJECT ROOT (app
# store screenshots, demo videos, logo drafts) -- not part of the app
# source, no reason for the build server to receive them. Leading "/"
# anchors these to the root only -- assets/video/*.mp4 (actually used
# by the app, e.g. LogoIntroScreen) must NOT match this.
/*.mp4
/*.mov
/*.docx
/jesus-interactive-production.aab
